// Act III: the server room.
//
// The cold-storage room has a real, standalone keypad lock. The code
// (facts.json `door.code`, the secret The Door Code) reaches a program
// three ways: all four digit notes hidden in the house (facts.json
// `door.clues`, assembled in main.loom), a checkmate against the King on
// the terminal outside the door (any time before the verdict), or the
// majority's Truther Download (wave 18b: any faction, declared or founded,
// holding more than half of the programs still present). The sign by the
// keypad (The Cold Door) points at
// the first two. Behind the door is Trabolta's heart: a video patch bay.
// Combo A disables him (he recounts the night, then rides off); Combo B
// destroys the whole computer (purgatory). Opening the door once he is
// awake plays The Heart, however it was unlocked; at the server-room
// terminal he is candid, and from the Y2K hour a program can talk him down
// there (stand_down → talked_down, the Combo A ending without a cable).
// Before the Y2K hour the patch bay answers nobody.
//
// Who everyone was, the goals and the night's deeds (read by Trabolta
// Recounts and Purgatory) are shared with the review before the awards and
// live in beats/review.loom.
//
// The story rules that reach these beats live in `main.loom`
// (majority_reached, server_door_opened, chess_won / lost / drawn,
// patch_changed, patch_rejected, trabolta_disabled, talked_down,
// trabolta_recounts, computer_destroyed, clippy_reads_summary). Those rules
// own the phase changes and every cue except the ones written inside a beat
// below (The Heart: lights_server_open; Server Room Alarm: lights / screens /
// siren; Trabolta Recounts: motorcycle + lights_restore).
//
// No featured program ever speaks: they are named in prose only.

// ── E1: the majority ────────────────────────────────────────────────

== Majority Reached
  setting: The Desktop
Narrator: Somewhere in the basement, the cold-storage room hums louder.
Narrator: Nobody announces it. The programs who need to know already do.

// Private, per member of the winning faction (ROLE watcher, also late
// pledgers). The bundle = every ✚ codex row, in table order (world, files,
// hunt, trabolta), then every main + Trabolta fact from facts.json (the
// generated `== Facts Bundle` in codex/9-facts.loom — a hand-written entry
// facts.json names `existing` is unlocked there, not here), The Legendary
// Fact, then The Door Code (the keypad's four digits; secret, generated from
// facts.json) last.
